laurel 2976: kept pool buffers go back only when that helps, and only what the request needs (laurel_gpu_kept_core.h). Fixes 2974: a request over the chunk room or a fragmented pool gave back all kept buffers, the window server's too, and the log said "the pool is empty"; fixes 2916 at gemNew: under the 64 MiB floor each ask gave back all kept buffers of all clients. A pool buffer with a live user mapping waits off the GPU tables until the descriptor has no other retain: its bytes never go to another client (Turnip unmaps before GEM close [V], the kernel does not rely on that). Lines: LAUREL GPU KEPT: no free range holds B bytes: K KiB of kept buffers gave way; LAUREL GPU KEPT: under the 64 MiB floor: ...; LAUREL GPU POOL: a buffer of B bytes at A waits: a user mapping is still there. Host test scripts/laurel/gpu-push-test.sh.

